    "name": "I \u2014 claymation-style stop motion on sports analysis (transformation reveal)",
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "nd_M5A8K9T5JQD115J26V7SJ8FMB7",
        "kind": "prompt",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 400
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "SHORT-FORM BRIEF \u2014 edit before running.\nFormat: claymation-style stop motion\nTopic: sports analysis\nHook (first 1.5s): [one line]\nPayoff: [one line]\nOn-screen text: [exact copy or leave blank]\nRuntime: 6s, 9:16, sound-on by default."
        },
        "name": "Short-form brief"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_1TYB9E5FY5XTZJ36PV1G7A656H",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 1 \u2014 format-native hook planning. The first 1.5 seconds carry the whole retention load."
        },
        "name": "Stage 1"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_QXXPX4FJ1XD11EKTVN9CS6RQNZ",
        "kind": "sticky-note",
        "position": {
          "x": 2100,
          "y": -60
        },
        "config": {
          "text": "STAGE 2 \u2014 render, finish and collect. Built for 9:16 sound-on playback."
        },
        "name": "Stage 2"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_3K8AKRDRSE8ZJ86R1F5ZH35M42",
        "kind": "text-gen",
        "position": {
          "x": 700,
          "y": 400
        },
        "config": {
          "model": "gpt-5.5",
          "max_tokens": 1400,
          "temperature": 0.85,
          "system_prompt": "You are a short-form creative director writing a claymation-style stop motion about sports analysis for a vertical feed.\n\nRETENTION. The first 1.5 seconds must contain a visual question the viewer needs resolved. Plan an explicit beat every 2 to 3 seconds; nothing static may hold longer than that.\n\nFORMAT LAW. Honour the grammar of the claymation-style stop motion \u2014 its native framing, its edit rhythm, and the specific thing audiences expect from it. If the format loops, the last frame must match the first.\n\nCAMERA. Compose 9:16 with the action in the safe centre band. Use a dolly-out that opens the frame into its environment on a 200mm compression telephoto, framing with a stacked layered composition with three depth planes.\n\nLOOK AND SOUND. Light with tungsten practicals in frame carrying the warm layer; grade as a bleach-bypass look with crushed saturation and lifted contrast. Specify the sound design in one clause \u2014 what the viewer hears in the first second decides whether they stay.\n\nOUTPUT. The response must be a lone prompt paragraph \u2014 strip any header, numbering or sign-off."
        },
        "name": "Format director"
      },
      {
        "id": "nd_46VK5TD4082EP7ATQTTFZ3VCKV",
        "kind": "image-input",
        "position": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 700
